ce 'All 54 patients analyzed had heterozygous variants in TNFAIP3'; inheritance, ACMG criteria, functional evidence and pathogenicity are 'not reported' because the paper's variant statements are cohort-level ('35 distinct pathogenic variants') or list several values. parental_testing_statement is filled for patients 3 and 18 only, from the sentence that a parent carries low-frequency somatic mosaicism of TNFAIP3 in peripheral blood; the variant the parent carries is not identified, so inheritance stays 'not reported'. The two low-frequency somatic mosaicism individuals (p.Q760X and c.806-1G>T) are reported as not having HA20 and are not relatives of an in-scope person, so they got no rows; the mother of patient 3 and the father of patient 18 are in scope as relatives of patients and are recorded with zygosity 'mosaic'; the three asymptomatic heterozygous relatives ('three cases with heterozygous variants were asymptomatic') are not described individually, so they got no rows. disease_label_as_stated is the initial diagnosis printed for that patient in Supplementary Table 2, not the paper's disease name. 'Kawasaki disease' and 'PFAPA' are medical history, not 'recurrent infections'. HPO candidate labels and identifiers were left null because no match was certain. is_proband is false with no span because the paper never uses the words proband or index case.",
